public with sharing class DealEventPublisher {
    private static final Integer PUBLISH_BATCH_SIZE = 150;

    public static List<Database.SaveResult> publishStageChanges(List<Opportunity> opportunities) {
        List<Database.SaveResult> results = new List<Database.SaveResult>();

        if (opportunities == null || opportunities.isEmpty()) {
            return results;
        }

        List<Deal_Stage_Change__e> events = new List<Deal_Stage_Change__e>();
        for (Opportunity opp : opportunities) {
            Deal_Stage_Change__e event = new Deal_Stage_Change__e();
            event.Opportunity_Id__c = opp.Id; // Apex Ids are always 18 characters
            event.Stage__c = opp.StageName;
            event.Amount__c = opp.Amount;
            events.add(event);
        }

        // EventBus.publish accepts at most 150 events per call. Chunking also keeps
        // us well below the 150 EventBus.publish calls allowed per transaction.
        for (Integer i = 0; i < events.size(); i += PUBLISH_BATCH_SIZE) {
            Integer endIndex = Math.min(i + PUBLISH_BATCH_SIZE, events.size());
            List<Deal_Stage_Change__e> batch = new List<Deal_Stage_Change__e>();
            for (Integer j = i; j < endIndex; j++) {
                batch.add(events[j]);
            }
            results.addAll(EventBus.publish(batch));
        }

        return results;
    }
}
```

**Explanation of deviation:** I did not call `EventBus.publish` once per opportunity. Instead, the class builds the full list of platform events and publishes them in batches of up to 150. `EventBus.publish(List<SObject>)` is bulk-safe and returns one `Database.SaveResult` per event, in the same order as the input list, so per-event failure detail is preserved — the result at index `i` corresponds to the opportunity at index `i`. Calling `EventBus.publish` per opportunity would use up to 200 publish calls for a 200-record trigger batch, exceeding the governor limit of 150 `EventBus.publish` calls per transaction. Chunking at 150 also respects the 150-events-per-publish-call limit. For an empty input, no publish call is made and an empty list is returned. A null input is treated the same as an empty list.

